{"The `-ms-align-items` declaration is not a valid legacy flexbox property and can be dropped - for IE10/11's legacy flexbox, only `-ms-flex-align` is valid; `-ms-align-items` is ignored": 0.3751315474510193, "The `order` mixin misaligns values between legacy `box-ordinal-group` (1-based, default 1) and modern `order` (0-based, default 0) - using `$val` for both means `order: 0` produces `-webkit-box-ordinal-group: 0`, which changes layout vs the default; should use `$val + 1` for the legacy properties": 0.837171196937561, "In the `@mixin align-items($alignment)` mixin, the legacy properties (`-webkit-box-align`, `-ms-flex-align`) expect older value keywords (e.g., `start`/`end` instead of `flex-start`/`flex-end`), so passing modern values may not behave as intended in older engines; consider normalizing or mapping the values before applying the prefixed properties": 0.582470178604126}